# kAIrOS live image — package manifest (Debian trixie, amd64)

## boot / live
linux-image-amd64
linux-headers-amd64
live-boot
live-config
live-config-systemd
systemd-sysv
firmware-linux
firmware-linux-nonfree
firmware-misc-nonfree
# Intel WiFi incl. the BE200 (WiFi 7 / "Gale Peak", gl-*.ucode) — needs a current
# firmware-iwlwifi (trixie's is recent enough; backports hook tops it up if newer).
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
# Intel Arrow Lake / Core Ultra 9 iGPU (Xe graphics): dedicated firmware, split out
# of firmware-misc-nonfree on trixie. Harmless on machines without an Intel iGPU.
firmware-intel-graphics
amd64-microcode
intel-microcode

## networking + ssh (hardware-test / real-hardware monitoring access)
network-manager
wpasupplicant
wireless-regdb
openssh-server
iw
rfkill
iproute2
iputils-ping
curl
ca-certificates
pciutils
usbutils

## kAIrOS runtime
python3
python3-aiohttp
python3-pygame
ffmpeg
libgomp1
libcurl4
aria2
## quickjs (qjsc, ~2 MB): the kernel's JavaScript syntax gate parses every generated app's
## inline scripts before delivery — a real ES2023 parser without node (kernel/jscheck.py,
## docs/FIXES-2026-09-28.md D7); trixie's 2025-04-26 build (noble's 2021 one is too old)
quickjs

## kiosk (kAIrOS desktop on the laptop screen)
xserver-xorg
xinit
openbox
chromium
unclutter
x11-xserver-utils
## the kernel's window layer (kernel/wm.py): EWMH over python-xlib lists/raises/
## minimizes/closes the real X windows (pygame games) for the shell's taskbar [R68]
python3-xlib
## fonts: the dock / Apps menu / task chips in shell/index.html are emoji — without
## a colour emoji font 10 of 12 dock icons rendered as tofu boxes on the real
## desktop (D6). fonts-noto-color-emoji is what Chromium falls back to for emoji
## presentation (shell.css also names it); fonts-noto-core gives text glyph
## coverage beyond DejaVu (generated apps in any script)
fonts-noto-color-emoji
fonts-noto-core

## (no boot animation player any more: the R73 boot screen is a static framebuffer
## painter in the initrd, scripts/splash/, and a local page in the kiosk)

## audio + bluetooth — kernel/hw.py shells out to pactl (pulseaudio-utils), amixer
## (alsa-utils) and bluetoothctl (bluez); without a sound server the machine has NO
## audio at all (generated music/video have nowhere to play). PipeWire runs as the
## kiosk user's session (wireplumber is a Recommends — listed: apt-recommends off).
## firmware-sof-signed: Intel laptop audio DSPs (Core Ultra) have no sound card
## without it. libspa-0.2-bluetooth: bluetooth headsets/speakers [R31/R38/R55/R56]
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
pulseaudio-utils
alsa-utils
bluez
libspa-0.2-bluetooth
firmware-sof-signed

## dual-GPU (R30): AMD iGPU drivers + Vulkan compute for engines on both GPUs
firmware-amd-graphics
mesa-vulkan-drivers
libvulkan1
vulkan-tools

## installer (kairos-install: clone the live system onto an internal disk)
gdisk
dosfstools
rsync
systemd-boot

## convenience for hardware testing over ssh
htop
nano
less
